{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303899-do-you-think-any-exalted-characters-are-strong-enough-to-become-planeswalkers-m-tg","id":1303899,"title":"Do you think any Exalted characters are strong enough to become Planeswalkers (M:TG)?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-10T01:11:46-07:00","id":1303899,"title":"Do you think any Exalted characters are strong enough to become Planeswalkers (M:TG)?","content":"A Planeswalker is, unsurprisingly, someone who can travel to other planes of existence. They are the most powerful people in the Magic: The Gathering's universe, and even some of the strongest mages/dragons/<b><i>lesser </i></b><b><i>deities</i></b> can be summoned by them to do battle. <br /> <br /> Who among the Exalted could be a Planeswalker? <b>Mask of Winters </b>certainly has the spellcasting chops to pull it off. <b>The Bishop </b>seems to possess the raw power to do it as well. Aside from the Deathlords, though, I'm stumped. Sidereals have the planes-jumping voodoo down pat but I doubt many have the strength to leave the world. At least <b>Chejop</b> could. <b>Brigid</b> seems like she would be up there with Urza and the other &quot;classic&quot; planeswalkers. Garruk is a Planeswalker who is Green Mana based (Nature, Beasts, Strength, Survival, Wilds, etc) so perhaps <b>Ma-Ha-Suchi</b>. <b>Her Redness</b> is definitely on the list, having the Time, Ability, and Resources to do it. In Hell we have <b>Octavian</b> for sheer power and maybe <b>Alveua</b> for ability. <b>Sigereth</b> might rather be summoned, ironically, and probably wouldn't be a planeswalker itself, but it easily could. <br /> <br /> Don't know many first age solars besides Brigid, and I don't think the new crop of Solaroids is there (yet!). I also don't know much about the Jadeborn, or the Dragon Kings. I'm going to rule out all of the Yozi (for being trapped), the Neverborn (for being unrealities), and the Incarnae (for being too intrinsic to the setting). Gaia, Autocthon, and Malfeas get the Yawgmoth treatment where they are basically a plane unto themselves rather than a planeswalker (the same is true in a lesser extent about the other yozi). <br /> <br /> So who would you add to the list?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T04:51:28-07:00","id":1303915,"title":"","content":"Planeswalkers have been generally depowered - some are still very potent mages, but other people are relatively one note like Chandra or Gideon. The <i>really</i> powerful ones tend to be beings that are powerful for other reasons, like Nicol Bolas the elder dragon.<br /> <br /> That said, in any crossover, you have to pick and choose what rules take precedence. For the purposes of this exercise, we'll say Creation is simply one of many planes in the multiverse, and while within Creation Exalted's rules and cosmology hold sway (and here, 'Creation' includes the Wyld, Malfeas, and the Underworld as linked shard-realms akin to the shards of Alara pre-Conflux). However, where planeswalking and the multiverse is concerned, the Magic lore is dominant.<br /> <br /> Technically, anyone could have a planeswalking spark, but it's a matter of having one and having a momentous event ignite it. Beings of pure mana cannot have a spark, and neither can artificial beings - although sparks can be transferred into one. So, for example, angels and demons cannot be planeswalkers, and neither can golems, but Karn the silver golem <i>is</i> a planeswalker due to housing a spark that was given to him (most recently, the one that used to belong to Venser.)<br /> <br /> So the immediate answer to your question is &quot;anyone&quot;, because innate power is not remotely a factor in having your spark ignite; you don't even need the heroism Exaltation requires. So instead, let's consider who would be interesting <i>as</i> a planeswalker.<br /> <br /> I'll rule out Exalted's demons for the same reason as any other demon, although an argument can be made they are different enough to have a spark (like the vampires of Innistrad, who are <i>technically</i> living beings, not undead and thus can be planeswalkers). Deathlords, same deal - they're dead, they don't get to have sparks now. Of the other characters you mention, the Scarlet Empress is certainly the most convenient. She's vanished mysteriously, who's to say she didn't just vanish into the crowds in Ravnica or explore Dominaria?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T05:04:02-07:00","id":1303919,"title":"","content":"I think planeswalkers still need to be magic users of some sort. <br /> <br /> I guess you could model them as a weird sort of exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T06:28:56-07:00","id":1303926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303899-do-you-think-any-exalted-characters-are-strong-enough-to-become-planeswalkers-m-tg?p=1303919#post1303919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think planeswalkers still need to be magic users of some sort.<br /> <br /> I guess you could model them as a weird sort of exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty generous with what counts as 'magic user'. Arilinn Kord is a werewolf. Garruk is mostly just a beefy nature shaman. Gideon only real magical trait is &quot;invulnerability&quot;, although he does technically know some law magic - he's actually a pretty good example of a Resistance Solar, come to think, given the way he fought the Eldrazi (big primordial cosmic horrors) was literally &quot;jump up in their face and hit them with my whip-sword&quot;. Kaya is a ghost assassin, which is to say, she assassinates ghosts. Samut doesn't really know any magic at all.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, they actually bear some resemblances to Exalted and how they can range from mystical masters of magical might, to &quot;hits people real good with a very large sword and doesn't fall down when they get hit in turn&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T06:39:23-07:00","id":1303927,"title":"","content":"Are we talking about the cool older planeswalkers were basically walking gods or the lame new planeswalkers who are just slightly better than normal mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T06:41:57-07:00","id":1303928,"title":"","content":"I honestly think current Planeswalkers are really pretty close to an Exigent type of their own. They pass on their sparks, have different types of magic that's good at different things, are uniquely special in certain ways, etc. The restriction on being a living being (with exceptions) also hits pretty close to an Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T07:29:59-07:00","id":1303938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303899-do-you-think-any-exalted-characters-are-strong-enough-to-become-planeswalkers-m-tg?p=1303927#post1303927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we talking about the cool older planeswalkers were basically walking gods or the lame new planeswalkers who are just slightly better than normal mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>For &quot;new&quot; read &quot;thing that is almost ten years old&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T07:48:02-07:00","id":1303941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303899-do-you-think-any-exalted-characters-are-strong-enough-to-become-planeswalkers-m-tg?p=1303938#post1303938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For &quot;new&quot; read &quot;thing that is almost ten years old&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has it been that long. I quit magic a while ago when those modern cards inflated in price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T08:06:43-07:00","id":1303946,"title":"","content":"I don't think sparks pass on by themselves, btw. They can be transferred, but that's pretty unusual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}